  "id": "psychometric-scaling",
  "term": "psychometric scaling",
  "definition": "Psychometric scaling is the method used to build and score a subjective measure, including how items are selected, what response options are used, and how scores are calculated. In assessment, it is part of the methodological development of a measure and supports later evaluation of how reliably, validly, and sensitively the measure performs.",
